<title>POLAND: POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 1.0 PCT IN SEPT 21-30.</title>
<headline>POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 1.0 PCT IN SEPT 21-30.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 1.0</p>
<p>percent in the September 21-30 period after rising 1.3 percent</p>
<p>in the previous 10 days and were 3.7 percent higher than in the</p>
<p>August 21-30 period, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>				  SEPT 21-30  SEPT 11-20   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p> POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)     1.0	   1.3	 3.7   (2.6)</p>
<p>  Bread			     0.2	   0.1	 0.5   (0.4)</p>
<p>  Fruit and vegetables	  4.0	   3.8	 5.7  (-6.7)</p>
<p>  Meat and meat-products	1.4	   2.6	 7.9   (8.2)</p>
<p>  Dairy products		  0.2	   0.2	 0.6   (0.6)</p>
<p>  Eggs				0.7	   1.0	 0.7   (7.4)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period</p>
<p>ending on September 20.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
